          ],
          "content": "9. Suppose the ‘+’ and ‘–’ symbols cannot be read on a battery. Suggest a method to identify the two terminals of this battery."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.446,
            0.744,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "10. You are given six cells marked $\\mathrm { A } _ { i }$ B, C, D, E, and F. Some of these are working and some are not. Design an activity to identify which of them are working."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.508,
            0.502,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "(i) List the items that you require."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.531,
            0.599,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Write the procedure that you will follow."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.556,
            0.743,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": "(iii) With the items, carry out the activity to identify the cells that are working."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.598,
